title    Neon Loop
composer Claude
about    An 8-bar K-pop chorus loop on the four-chord vi-IV-I-V progression in C major (Am F C G), driven by an eighth-note synth bass and four-on-the-floor drums.
tempo    120
beats    4
steps    4

# Harmony plan: one chord per bar, Am | F | C | G, played twice.
# The vi-IV-I-V order gives the bittersweet minor-start lift typical of K-pop choruses.

# pad: sustained wash an octave above the bass. Voicings sit in G3..B4 and move
# by step so the chords glide; upper extensions (9ths, maj7) over the bass root
# give the glossy "Am9 / Fmaj9" colour without crowding the low end.
voice pad   pad      vol=0.55 pan=-0.25
# stab: bright saw chord stabs in a 3-3-4-3-3 syncopated rhythm, the rhythmic hook
# of the chorus. Close triads in E4..C5, above the pad, panned opposite it.
voice stab  saw      vol=0.5  pan=0.3  gate=0.7
# bass: the driving synth bass. Straight eighths with octave pops and a 16th push
# in the middle of each bar; short gate so each note punches. Roots stay A1..C2.
voice bass  synbass  vol=1.0  gate=0.75
# drums: four-on-the-floor kick, clap+snare backbeat, 16th closed hats with
# ghosted steps, open hat on every offbeat eighth for the dance-pop pulse.
voice kick  kick     vol=1.1
voice clap  clap     vol=0.8
voice snare snare    vol=0.55
voice hat   hat      vol=0.45
voice ohat  ohat     vol=0.4
voice crash crash    vol=0.6

pattern chorus
# Am9 (over A bass)         Fmaj9 (over F)           C                        Gsus4 -> G
pad   | C4+E4+G4+B4--------------- | A3+C4+E4+G4--------------- | G3+C4+E4+G4--------------- | G3+C4+D4+G4------- G3+B3+D4+G4------- |
pad   | C4+E4+G4+B4--------------- | A3+C4+E4+G4--------------- | G3+C4+E4+G4--------------- | G3+C4+D4+G4------- G3+B3+D4+G4------- |
stab  | E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- .. E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- . | F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- .. F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- . | E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- .. E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- . | D4+G4+B4- . D4+G4+B4- . D4+G4+B4- .. D4+G4+B4- . D4+G4+B4- . |
# second half: last stab of bar 8 climbs to D5 on top to pull back into the loop
stab  | E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- .. E4+A4+C5- . E4+A4+C5- . | F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- .. F4+A4+C5- . F4+A4+C5- . | E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- .. E4+G4+C5- . E4+G4+C5- . | D4+G4+B4- . D4+G4+B4- . D4+G4+B4- .. G4+B4+D5- . G4+B4+D5-! . |
# bass: root eighths, octave pop on beat 2-and, 16th push, and a fifth/approach at the end
bass  | A1-! A1- A2- A1 A1 .- A1-! A2- E2- | F1-! F1- F2- F1 F1 .- F1-! F2- C2- | C2-! C2- C3- C2 C2 .- C2-! C3- G2- | G1-! G1- G2- G1 G1 .- G1-! G2- D2- |
# bar 8 bass walks G-A-B up into the Am downbeat
bass  | A1-! A1- A2- A1 A1 .- A1-! A2- E2- | F1-! F1- F2- F1 F1 .- F1-! F2- C2- | C2-! C2- C3- C2 C2 .- C2-! C3- G2- | G1-! G1- G2- G1 G1 .- G1-! A1- B1- |
kick  | X... x... X... x... | % | % | % | % | % | % | X... x... X... x.x. |
clap  | .... X... .... X... | % | % | % | % | % | % | % |
# snare doubles the clap, then a short roll in bar 8 as the turnaround fill
snare | .... x... .... x... | % | % | % | % | % | % | .... x... ..x. xXxX |
hat   | xo.o xo.o xo.o xo.o | % | % | % | % | % | % | % |
ohat  | ..x. ..x. ..x. ..x. | % | % | % | % | % | % | % |
# crash marks the top of each four-bar phrase
crash | X... .... .... .... | _ | _ | _ | X... .... .... .... | _ | _ | _ |

loop chorus
